Cell["Basic Examples", "Subsection",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->904125756,ExpressionUUID->"8ad9d452-2e30-4456-a46b-e0afaf4735f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inner (Hestenes) product  is a product of multivectors a and b.  If  grades \
of two homogeneous multivectors coincide, inner product turns into scalar \
product. The StandardForm notation is \[InnerProduct] (unicode char \\ \
:0x2219, not to be confused with Dot[ ]). For nice input use keyboard alias \
\[EscapeKey]ip\[EscapeKey]. UnicodeSymbols.tr defines the following operation \
precedences: NonCommutativeMultiply (**, highest), Times (*, Space), \
RightContract (\[RightContract]), LeftContract (\[LeftContract]), \
InnerProduct (\[InnerProduct]), CommutativeProduct (\[CommutativeProduct]), \
OuterProduct (\[OuterProduct]), GeometricProduct(\[GeometricProduct]), Plus \
(lowest).. To demonstrate the action let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define some basis \
and two general multivectors ",
 StyleBox["mva", "CodeText"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["mvb", "CodeText"]
}], "Text",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.954599430847682*^9, 3.9545994368102837`*^9}, {
